From 4d1621c1c3bc734b9d0e267f0c906a59b5ff785f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jawad Amin <jawadamin@google.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 19:40:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] Add the DeepSeek V4.1 TPU attention, compressor and
 indexer

V4.1 keeps the class names of V4 but changes the compressor contract and
the layer topology, so the TPU custom ops go in a sibling package rather
than behind flags on the V4 ones.

The compressor implements the V4.1 math in JAX. Ratio 1 is an RMSNorm on
512 channels. Ratio 2 pools two rows with a per-channel softmax gate over
the trailing channels of the projection, and it keeps a float32 ring for
the groups that straddle a chunk boundary. Both write the packed record
that the tuned sparse-MLA kernel reads: 448 FP8 E4M3 values with 7 E8M0
block scales in the main array, and 64 BF16 rotary channels in the
companion array.

The indexer derives its keys from the compressor latent, which V4 did
not do, and rotates them at the group's first-token position.

The attention layer selects the compressed cache by the kv-source role
rather than by the compress ratio. V4.1 uses ratios 0, 1 and 2, so every
ratio test that V4 relies on is false for every layer, and a straight
copy would take the dense path with no error. An index source publishes
its top-k indices for the consumer layers below it, because the shared
in-place buffer of the CUDA path cannot work on the functional JAX path.

The runner's overlay planner now recognizes V4.1 and gives the split
NoPE and RoPE treatment to its kv-source layers. It also raises when a
page size is not a multiple of the row packing, which would otherwise
drop the last states of every page without an error.
